body:
@dimitris-athanasiou 

I confirm that I can execute your query through knn search (not knn query):

```js
POST example/_search
{
    "knn" : {
        "field": "nested_1.vector",
        "query_vector": [1, 2, 3],
        "filter": {
            "nested": {
                "path": "nested_2",
                "query": {
                    "term": {
                        "nested_2.category": {
                            "value": "label_1"
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Can you try using it instead of knn query. Nested knn query when executing sets the context of `nested_1` that's why your filter will not work as it will search in `nested_1.nested_2`. knn search doesn't do that.


----
```js
 PUT example
  {
      "mappings": {
          "properties": {
              "nested_items": {
                  "type": "nested",
                  "properties": {
                      "vector": {
                          "type": "dense_vector",
                          "dims": 3
                      },
                      "category": {
                          "type": "keyword"
                      }
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }

  Then query:

  POST example/_search
  {
      "query": {
          "nested": {
              "path": "nested_items",
              "query": {
                  "knn": {
                      "nested_items.vector": {
                          "query_vector": [1, 2, 3],
                          "k": 10,
                          "num_candidates": 10,
                          "filter": {
                              "term": {
                                  "nested_items.category": "label_1"
                              }
                          }
                      }
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
```
